Kount — "One collection per item" in the organisation vault's batch bar (plan claim-and-sso item 2 (a), D1, D10).

At web v2026.10.1 the organisation vault's bulk actions are the shared batch bar (`libs/vault` `VaultBatchBarService`), so the
entry is a batch-bar action shown only when the admin console's vault gives the bar its optional `splitCollections` callback
(every other host of the bar is unchanged). The assignment is the same `PUT /ciphers/<id>/collections-admin` as before, sent
through `ApiService.send` (upstream moved its own call into the SDK, whose errors carry no HTTP status). For each selected
login, in order: build the stamp `kp:new:<host>|<name>|<username>` (D1; conformance/stamp-vectors.json is the
contract), create a collection with the chosen name and the stamp as its External ID, then assign the login to it alone, which removes
it from every other collection. Kount Protect reads the stamps and claims them. Each write has three outcomes, and the
classification is total: done (a 2xx whose body yields what the next step needs), refused (a 4xx) and unknown (everything else,
since the server may have committed: docs/spike-2026-11.md S8). The first stop ends the run: earlier logins stay split, later ones
untouched, and only a refused assignment deletes anything (its collection, just made and empty). Cut against the tree with A1 and
P5 applied; applied in name order. Strings are English in the new files; an upstream PR would move them to messages.json.

